@startuml deployment-diagram
title UML Deployment Diagram - JobPortal BD (what the repository confirms about runtime)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

legend right
  Solid border / solid line : confirmed by code, scripts or configuration
  Dashed line / "unconfirmed" : not determinable from the repository
  The repository contains NO Dockerfile, docker-compose, CI/CD workflow,
  hosting manifest (Vercel, Netlify, Render, Procfile ...) or deployment documentation.
  Only local-development defaults are verifiable.
endlegend

node "User device" as device {
  node "Web browser" as browser <<execution environment>> {
    artifact "React SPA bundle\n(Client/ build or Vite dev output)" as spa
  }
}

node "Static asset host / Vite dev server" as webhost <<unconfirmed host>> {
  artifact "Client/\nnpm run dev (Vite, default :5173)\nnpm run build / preview" as clientsrc
}

node "Application host" as apphost <<unconfirmed host>> {
  node "Node.js runtime" as nodert <<execution environment>> {
    artifact "Server/server.js\n(npm start / dev = nodemon)\nExpress 5, port PORT (default 5000)\nroutes under BASE_URL = /api/v1" as api
    artifact "Server/utils/seed.js\n(npm run seed, one-off admin creation)" as seed
  }
}

node "Database host" as dbhost <<unconfirmed host>> {
  database "MongoDB\n(connection via MONGO_URI)\ncollections: users, jobs, applications" as mongo
}

cloud "Cloudinary (SaaS)" as cloud
cloud "Gmail SMTP (smtp.gmail.com:587)" as smtp

clientsrc ..> spa : served to browser
spa --> api : HTTP/REST (JSON, multipart)\nVITE_API_URL, default http://localhost:5000/api/v1\nCORS origin CLIENT_URL, default http://localhost:5173\ncredentials: include (cookie)
api --> mongo : MongoDB protocol (Mongoose)
seed ..> mongo : create first admin
api --> cloud : HTTPS (Cloudinary SDK)
api --> smtp : SMTP, STARTTLS (Nodemailer)

note bottom of apphost
  Whether web host, application host and database host are the same machine,
  separate servers or managed services (e.g. a hosted MongoDB) cannot be
  determined. server.js sets DNS resolvers 8.8.8.8 and 1.1.1.1, which suggests
  a DNS-based (possibly SRV) MongoDB connection string, but this is an inference only.
end note
note bottom of cloud
  Credentials for MongoDB, Cloudinary, SMTP and JWT come from environment variables
  (Server/.env, excluded by .gitignore). Values are intentionally not documented.
end note
@enduml
